      "latin": "operculum, operculī n.",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "classical",
      "comment": "Also covers a container’s cap, not only a blender lid; Morgan–Owens explicitly groups “lid, cap (of container).” For a cap worn on the head, see <span lang=\"la\">pilleus</span>.",
      "evidence": [
        "Traupman 298"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "phrases": [
    {
      "latin": "Operculum claude.",
      "english": "Close the lid.",
      "source": "composed"
    },
    {
      "latin": "Operculum impōne.",
      "english": "Put the lid / cap on.",
      "source": "composed"
    },
    {
      "latin": "Dōnec māchina movērī dēsierit, operculum nōlī aperīre.",
      "english": "Don’t open the lid until the machine has stopped moving.",
      "source": "composed"
    },
    {
      "latin": "Operculum inpōnitō, relinquitō quā interspīret.",
      "english": "Put the lid on, and leave a gap for it to breathe.",
